==========================================
DAY 28 NOTES — Log Analysis for Security
Date: 26-09-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- Real investigation = confirm activity exists -> identify source -> count frequency -> check for success
- "47 failures then 1 success from the same IP" is a textbook brute-force compromise pattern
- Combining grep + regex (Day 26) + sort/uniq -c gives a ranked list of worst-offending IPs
- Always check for "Accepted password" from a suspicious IP to confirm/rule out compromise
- Building a full timeline (grep "<ip>" auth.log) shows the complete story of an IP's activity
- A repeatable process (checklist or script) beats manually eyeballing logs each time

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] grep -c "Failed password" (confirm activity)
[ ] grep + regex extraction of IPs
[ ] sort | uniq -c | sort -rn (ranking offenders)
[ ] checking for "Accepted password" from a specific IP
[ ] building a full timeline for one IP

fill this in after running commands yourself :
$ sudo grep -c "Failed password" /var/log/auth.log
